# React Component Patterns

## shadcn/ui Conventions

- Primitives live in `src/components/ui/` (Button, Dialog, Input, etc.)
- Use `class-variance-authority` (cva) for variant-based styling
- Compose with `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` (wraps `clsx` + `tailwind-merge`)
- Never modify ui/ primitives directly; extend via wrapper components

## Component Structure

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"

interface Props {
  className?: string
  children: React.ReactNode
}

export function MyComponent({ className, children }: Props) {
  return <div className={cn("base-classes", className)}>{children}</div>
}
```

## Rules

- Functional components only, no class components
- Props interface defined inline or co-located (not in a separate types file unless shared)
- Use `"use client"` only when the component needs browser APIs, hooks, or event handlers
- Server Components by default in App Router pages
- Extract reusable logic into custom hooks in `src/hooks/`
- Colocate feature-specific components near their route

## Radix UI Integration

- Import from `@radix-ui/react-*` packages
- Always forward `ref` when wrapping Radix primitives
- Use Radix's built-in accessibility (keyboard nav, focus management, ARIA)
- Animations via `tailwindcss-animate` plugin + `data-[state=open/closed]` selectors
